# LTL331 NEPC — Intel-Mac LOCAL exploration env (CPU-only)
# Slimmer than requirements.in for fast install on a laptop.
#
# Hardware target: Intel x86_64 macOS, no NVIDIA / no MPS / AMD not ML-usable.
# Everything below installs cleanly via uv/pip on this platform.
# Use with:
#   uv venv .venv --python 3.11
#   source .venv/bin/activate
#   uv pip install -r env/requirements-local.in
#   uv pip freeze > env/requirements-local.txt    # capture the actual resolved versions

# --- core ---
numpy
scipy
pandas
scikit-learn
matplotlib
seaborn
statsmodels
anndata
scanpy
pyyaml

# --- trajectory ---
scvelo                     # dynamical recover_dynamics is slow on CPU (~30-60 min on 51k cells)
cellrank>=2.0

# --- notebooks ---
marimo

# --- optimal-transport / RealTimeKernel (uses JAX; CPU only on Intel Mac) ---
# Uncomment when you want to run the moscot RealTimeKernel locally.
# JAX x86-macOS wheels are still published but on a deprecation track;
# pin the resolved versions in requirements-local.txt for reproducibility.
# moscot[scrnaseq]

# --- patient-level stats Stack C accelerators (Intel-Mac safe; no torch) ---
# Add these to upgrade patient_level_stats.py beyond the self-contained fallbacks.
# celltypist
# decoupler
# scib

# --- intentionally NOT installed locally ---
# pertpy / scvi-tools / pyscenic — pull in PyTorch / heavy deps; run on the server.
